<urn:atm:triage:finding/AV-HOTFIX-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AV-HOTFIX-002" ;
  triage:title "rand-m4 production trust store carries a stale duplicate host entry, a fixture host, and a LAN-IP advertised identity, violating the single-hostname trust-key requirement" ;
  triage:description "rand-m4's trust store contains stale and fixture host entries that violate the documented single-hostname-per-peer requirement. Specifically: 'Rands-MacBook-M5.local' (fingerprint C7E35D64) is a stale leftover from before the M5 host rename (2026-08-03), already manually revoked by Rand on rand-m4 -- see correction note below; 'rand-m5' (fingerprint BFCA33B6) is the correct live entry; 'peer.example.test' is a fixture host that must not be present in a production trust store; rand-m4 also advertises its own identity via a LAN IP rather than a stable hostname, which independently violates ADR-040's stable-hostname requirement. Cross-checked against rand-m5's own trust config: rand-m5 advertises as 'rand-m5.local' with correct fingerprint BFCA33B6, confirming rand-m4's 'rand-m5' entry is correct. CORRECTED remediation (Rand, relayed via fenix, 2026-09-05T18:36Z): the 'localhost' entry on each host is REQUIRED for loopback delivery and must NOT be removed -- drop that item from the original remediation. Corrected remediation: remove C7E35D64 (stale, already done), remove peer.example.test (fixture), switch rand-m4's advertised identity from its LAN IP to a stable hostname, retain BFCA33B6 rand-m5 and localhost." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-av" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "documentation" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T21:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T19:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AV4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T18:10:49Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AV-HOTFIX-002/AV-HOTFIX-002-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

# NOTE (2026-09-05, team-lead, out-of-band manual action + correction):
# (1) Rand directed fenix to manually revoke the stale
# 'Rands-MacBook-M5.local' trust entry (fingerprint C7E35D64) on rand-m4's
# live trust store, ahead of any code fix landing.
# (2) CORRECTION (Rand, relayed via fenix, 2026-09-05T18:36Z): the
# 'localhost' trust entry on each host is REQUIRED for loopback delivery
# and must stay -- it was wrongly listed as a removal item in the original
# triage pass. That item is superseded; see the corrected remediation in
# the description field above. Remaining open items: peer.example.test
# fixture removal, and rand-m4 advertising a LAN IP instead of a stable
# hostname (new fact from Rand, no file/line occurrence yet identified).
# This note does not change triage:status/dispatchReady -- closure remains
# quality-mgr's call once the remaining items are verified fixed.

# RULINGS (Rand, relayed via fenix, 2026-09-05T19:05Z) -- approved fix scope,
# still triage:dispatchReady false pending consolidation with other approved
# cross-host items onto one fix branch (no per-finding worktrees):
# 1. APPROVED: `atm peer trust add`/`replace` must validate the fingerprint
#    is exactly 64 hex characters and reject anything else; `atm doctor`
#    must flag any malformed fingerprint already present in the store. Live
#    evidence for the bug: rand-m4's trust list holds host
#    'peer.example.test' with fingerprint 'sha256:test-peer' -- not a valid
#    64-hex value -- proving today's add/replace path accepts malformed
#    fingerprints unvalidated.
# 2. APPROVED: tests must never run against the live atm database. Use an
#    in-RAM SQLite database for unit tests, or a test-owned temp directory
#    with guaranteed delete hygiene; every test touching the trust store (or
#    any store) must run under an isolated home. Find the specific
#    test/smoke path that wrote 'peer.example.test' into the real ~/.atm
#    store and add a guard so a fixture host can never land in the real
#    store again.
# 3. SUPERSEDED by addendum below (2026-09-05T19:07Z) -- a doctor warning
#    for bare-IP advertise_host is now approved scope; see item 5.
# 4. Manual live cleanup on rand-m4 (revoke peer.example.test trust entry;
#    change advertise_host from 192.168.128.82 to rand-m4.local) was
#    assigned by Rand to team-lead@rand-m5, not this (rand-m4) session --
#    tracked there, not duplicated here. Do NOT touch either host's
#    localhost trust entry; it carries that host's own cert and is required
#    for loopback.
# 5. ADDENDUM (Rand, relayed via fenix, 2026-09-05T19:07Z), approved fix
#    scope: a bare-IP advertise_host is APPROVED as a doctor WARNING only --
#    flag it for cleanup and suggest a host name -- and must NOT be
#    prohibited or rejected anywhere else (config load, peer interface add,
#    and the send path must all keep accepting a bare-IP advertise_host).
# Items 1, 2, and 5 above are approved fix scope for code changes
# (fingerprint validation + test isolation guard + bare-IP advertise_host
# doctor warning); dispatch remains held pending consolidation onto one fix
# branch with other approved cross-host items.

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AV-HOTFIX-002/AV-HOTFIX-002-1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "docs/adr/ADR-040-peer-authority-resolution.md" ;
  triage:line 16 ;
  triage:snippet "A cross-host peer is registered by a stable hostname, HTTPS port, and pinned certificate fingerprint. The durable record stores only that endpoint identity and pin; it never stores a resolved IP alias." ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:branch "integrate/phase-av" ;
  triage:headSha "9a810ab29743e0f11b71881d8c3d359ad8d1b9ca" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate/phase-av/9a810ab29743e0f11b71881d8c3d359ad8d1b9ca> .

<urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate/phase-av/9a810ab29743e0f11b71881d8c3d359ad8d1b9ca>
  a triage:WorktreeSnapshot ;
  triage:path ".worktrees/integrate-phase-av" ;
  triage:branch "integrate/phase-av" ;
