  triage:orderIndex 1 .

# quality-mgr, 2026-09-05, qa-pr1220-r1: closing this record for the
# approved code-scope items (1, 2, 5) confirmed on fix/av-hotfix-crosshost
# @ 295ae10d4 (PR #1220). Item 4 (manual live cleanup on rand-m4) remains
# assigned to team-lead@rand-m5 and is NOT closed by this record.
# 1. crates/atm/src/commands/peer.rs:453-455 -- trust add/replace requires
#    exactly 64 hex chars; test trust_add_and_replace_require_exactly_64_hex_fingerprint_characters.
#    crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs:307-340 -- malformed_fingerprint_findings
#    flags any malformed fingerprint already in the store.
# 2. Independently swept all 8 occurrences of the literal "peer.example.test"
#    across the worktree (client.rs, doctor.rs, recipient.rs, post_write_tests.rs,
#    provenance.rs, address.rs, ack/mod.rs, send/tests.rs): every one is an
#    in-memory fixture/RecordingConnector/tempdir()-backed TestRuntime, never a
#    default/home-relative store. scripts/smoke/ has zero references to the
#    string or to "peer trust add". No path that writes this fixture into the
#    real ~/.atm store remains.
# 5. crates/atm/src/commands/peer.rs:182-206 (InterfaceSubcommand::Set never
#    calls is_durable_hostname() on advertise_host) + doctor/mod.rs:325-341
#    (literal_advertise_host_findings, warning-level only) + zero matches for
#    advertise_host in crates/atm/src/commands/send.rs -- bare-IP
#    advertise_host is a doctor WARNING only, never rejected at config load,
#    peer-interface-add, or send.
# localhost trust entries confirmed untouched.

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AV-HOTFIX-002/AV-HOTFIX-002-fixed-295ae10d4>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm/src/commands/peer.rs" ;
  triage:line 453 ;
  triage:snippet "fingerprint length==64 && all ascii_hexdigit validated on trust add/replace; literal-IP advertise_host accepted everywhere, flagged only as a doctor warning" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:branch "fix/av-hotfix-crosshost" ;
